{"id":"c25618a32d1c10c9","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-thm-shelah-pcf.md","title":"Shelah's pcf Maximum Theorem","display":"thm-shelah-pcf — Shelah's pcf Maximum Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-shelah-pcf","aliases":["58-thm-shelah-pcf"],"display":"thm-shelah-pcf — Shelah's pcf Maximum Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","[[58-df-pcf]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-shelah-pcf"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-shelah-pcf</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-shelah-pcf — Shelah's pcf Maximum Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b82cea6742372d50\" href=\"?note=b82cea6742372d50\" title=\"58-df-pcf\">58-df-pcf</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-shelah-pcf-—-Shelah's-pcf-Theorem\">thm-shelah-pcf — Shelah's pcf Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> (nonempty progressive set of regular cardinals)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\)</span> (set of possible cofinalities)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> (regular-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}regular\\text{-}set} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\ne\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}regular\\text{-}set} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\ne\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\le\\lambda)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\le\\lambda)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The core pcf theorem used here is that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\)</span> has a largest member when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is progressive.</li>\n<li>The former blanket bound <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pp}(\\kappa)&lt;\\beth_\\kappa\">\\(\\mathrm{pp}(\\kappa)&lt;\\beth_\\kappa\\)</span> was not an appropriate statement of Shelah's pcf theorem.</li>\n<li>pcf theory yields strong restrictions on singular-cardinal arithmetic without deciding every singular power.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-shelah-pcf-—-Shelah's-pcf-Theorem","text":"thm-shelah-pcf — Shelah's pcf Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"b82cea6742372d50","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-pcf]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S$ (regular-cardinal predicate, see [[58-df-regular-cardinal]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}regular\\text{-}set} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\ne\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\land|A|<\\min A","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProgressiveRegularSet}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\le\\lambda)","display":true},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{pp}(\\kappa)<\\beth_\\kappa","display":false}],"bytes":1348,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4414","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-thm-shelah-pcf.md|58-thm-shelah-pcf]]（